<title>USA: U.S. Q2 corporate profits fell 0.3 pct.</title>
<headline>U.S. Q2 corporate profits fell 0.3 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-08-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commerce Department preliminary estimates of second quarter profits by U.S. corporations, with comparisons. Profits before tax include inventory valuation and capital consumption adjustments.</p>
<p>Data are chain weighted and expressed in seasonally adjusted annual rates of billions of dollars, with second quarter percent changes from the first quarter.</p>
<p> -		  Pct--Q2'96-P---Q1'96-Rev from---1995</p>
<p> -  After Tax  -0.3   407.4    408.8    415.6   380.2</p>
<p> -  Before Tax  1.3   653.8    645.1    652.0   586.6</p>
<p> Tax Liability  1.4   236.7    233.4    233.4   218.7</p>
<p>The last time corporate profits declined was in the second quarter of 1995, when they fell 0.5 percent, the department said.</p>
